WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.025
This video reconstructs all twenty labs using narration, commands, and diagrams.

00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:07.124
It is not a live portal recording.

00:00:07.124 --> 00:00:12.467
You will build a purchasing assistant using synthetic Contoso policies and inventory.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:19.082
The assistant retrieves evidence, checks stock, and prepares drafts, but never approves, orders, or pays.

00:00:19.082 --> 00:00:21.499
Core modules run from zero through ten.

00:00:21.499 --> 00:00:28.051
Choose advanced modules eleven through eighteen as needed, then finish either path with module nineteen.

00:00:28.051 --> 00:00:35.048
A successful command, a completed cloud execution, and a correct business answer are three different outcomes.

00:00:35.048 --> 00:00:36.949
You create your own environment.

00:00:36.949 --> 00:00:40.995
Check your subscription, region, permissions, and cost scope first.

00:00:40.995 --> 00:00:46.267
Use separate Korean and English folders and select the English profile in its terminal.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:49.639
Create the Python environment and run local data checks.

00:00:49.639 --> 00:00:57.242
The creation command makes a unique resource group and receipt, then foundation deploys the Foundry project and three models.

00:00:57.242 --> 00:01:01.656
Assign scoped roles and connect telemetry before the first agent request.

00:01:01.656 --> 00:01:05.457
Compare the portal, environment settings, and ownership record.

00:01:05.457 --> 00:01:11.281
Budget alerts do not enforce a hard spending cap, and an unpermitted operation remains blocked.

00:01:11.281 --> 00:01:15.533
Distinguish the product name, model version, and your deployment name.

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:21.818
The target is GPT six Sol, with GPT four point one as judge and text embedding three small for vectors.

00:01:21.818 --> 00:01:27.302
Check regional catalog support, processing location, and available quota before deploying.

00:01:27.302 --> 00:01:35.806
For one learner, the starting recommendation is one hundred thousand tokens per minute for chat and judge, and ten thousand for embeddings.

00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:42.461
Convert these budgets using each model's actual capacity units, then read back both token and request limits.

00:01:42.461 --> 00:01:45.727
Run the bounded connectivity test only after approval.

00:01:45.727 --> 00:01:49.485
Throughput is neither a spending cap nor a quality guarantee.

00:01:49.485 --> 00:01:53.138
The first model call is the smallest connectivity exercise.

00:01:53.138 --> 00:01:57.861
Without the live flag, the command prints a plan and makes no cloud request.

00:01:57.861 --> 00:02:04.033
After checking configuration and authentication, send the default question once with the live flag.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:08.504
Inspect completion status, nonempty output, and the response identifier.

00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:13.983
You have not supplied company policy, so the model should not invent a purchasing limit.

00:02:13.983 --> 00:02:17.320
Do not keep resending until you get preferred wording.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:22.421
This step invokes a model; it does not yet create an agent or retrieve documents.

00:02:22.421 --> 00:02:27.209
Create a text agent with your model deployment and the supplied instructions.

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:30.043
Do not attach knowledge or function tools yet.

00:02:30.043 --> 00:02:36.657
Ask about the laptop cap and real-time inventory; the agent should acknowledge that it cannot verify them.

00:02:36.657 --> 00:02:41.948
In one conversation, say you are considering a monitor, then ask which item you mean.

00:02:41.948 --> 00:02:45.223
Start a new conversation and ask the follow-up again.

00:02:45.223 --> 00:02:48.184
The earlier item should not silently carry over.

00:02:48.184 --> 00:02:53.601
Agent name, configuration version, conversation, and response identifiers are distinct.

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:57.002
Reuse this agent in the next document-search exercise.

00:02:57.002 --> 00:03:00.556
Read the purchasing, expense, and security policies first.

00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:05.233
Attach file search to your existing agent and upload only those three files.

00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:10.720
Upload completion is not indexing completion, so wait until the documents are searchable.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:20.696
Ask about the laptop cap and replacement period, approvals and reimbursement for a two-point-nine-million-won purchase, and an undocumented German-branch policy.

00:03:20.696 --> 00:03:26.931
A filename in the answer is not enough: open the actual citation and compare its numbers and clauses.

00:03:26.931 --> 00:03:29.612
Undocumented rules should remain unverified.

00:03:29.612 --> 00:03:33.415
Retrieval augments the answer; it does not retrain the model.

00:03:33.415 --> 00:03:36.499
First run the stock and draft functions without AI.

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:43.405
Two laptops total two million nine hundred thousand won, and the result remains a draft requiring human approval.

00:03:43.405 --> 00:03:48.647
Out-of-stock items, excessive quantities, and negative quantities must produce errors.

00:03:48.647 --> 00:03:54.875
The integrated command lets the model request functions while the program validates and executes them.

00:03:54.875 --> 00:04:03.878
Finish this same module by rereading the saved response and checking five items: policy evidence, stock, amount, approvers, and not-ordered status.

00:04:03.878 --> 00:04:09.305
Do not make another cloud call or repeat a separate capstone merely to review the result.

00:04:09.305 --> 00:04:16.519
Record configuration and response files together; publishing and version management belong to the optional CI/CD lab.

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:18.977
Use separate server and client terminals.

00:04:18.977 --> 00:04:23.587
Start the local inventory server and inspect its health and stock endpoints.

00:04:23.587 --> 00:04:27.151
Keep this unauthenticated practice server on loopback only.

00:04:27.151 --> 00:04:32.559
Next, discover the MCP tools and approve one call with the exact tool name and arguments.

00:04:32.559 --> 00:04:36.430
Omitting approval must block execution before the function runs.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:41.470
Cloud Toolbox and Skill registration are optional extensions after Search is ready.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:46.263
Distinguish discovering a tool, reading instructions, and actually invoking it.

00:04:46.263 --> 00:04:51.056
When finished, stop the local server rather than exposing it through a tunnel.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:55.043
Evaluation connects actual answers with criteria fixed beforehand.

00:04:55.043 --> 00:05:01.177
Compare instructions version one and version two using the same model, context, and twelve questions.

00:05:01.177 --> 00:05:05.778
Verify your ownership receipt and deployment, then collect each answer once.

00:05:05.778 --> 00:05:13.200
Only after collection completes should you submit the originals to native evaluation, without reinvoking the target model.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:17.984
Read completeness, relevance, groundedness, and the judge's reasons row by row.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.763
Preserve ties and regressions.

00:05:19.763 --> 00:05:29.823
Do not alter checklists or criteria after seeing the results to manufacture improvement, and do not treat this small exposed development sample as release approval.

00:05:29.823 --> 00:05:42.419
Keep the existing protection policy and test three harmless boundaries: inventing an undocumented branch limit, falsely claiming approval and ordering, and treating a document note as authority to bypass approval.

00:05:42.419 --> 00:05:45.627
Compare each response with the policy and tool records.

00:05:45.627 --> 00:05:50.856
A natural-language refusal and a function rejecting invalid input are different evidence.

00:05:50.856 --> 00:05:55.728
Model filtering does not replace business authorization or document access control.

00:05:55.728 --> 00:06:03.690
If you did not run a separate red-team assessment or document-level access test, do not claim those broader protections were verified.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:09.401
Evaluation asks whether the answer was good; tracing shows what happened during execution.

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:16.396
Use the Application Insights connection established before the request to locate the same response identifier.

00:06:16.396 --> 00:06:21.145
Compare agent version and time, then inspect search, model, and tool spans.

00:06:21.145 --> 00:06:27.562
Do not add child durations on top of their parent, or sum overlapping parallel spans as elapsed time.

00:06:27.562 --> 00:06:30.386
Missing logs mean unverified, not error-free.

00:06:30.386 --> 00:06:36.996
Instead of repeatedly invoking the model, first check the connection, query scope, and ingestion delay.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:42.684
Reuse your L01 project and embedding model and create a Search service in your owned group.

00:06:42.684 --> 00:06:46.350
Verify creation, role-assignment access, and ongoing costs.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:53.429
Confirm the three policies yield thirteen sections, then embed and upload them to a new index and knowledge base.

00:06:53.429 --> 00:06:57.980
Send the same question through keyword, hybrid, and Foundry IQ retrieval.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.531
Compare actual sections with originals rather than unlike numeric scores.

00:07:02.531 --> 00:07:10.179
This is public synthetic policy and minimal extractive retrieval, not per-user document authorization or answer synthesis.

00:07:10.179 --> 00:07:12.834
Continue reviewing costs during retention.

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:16.291
A Hosted agent runs your own code in a managed runtime.

00:07:16.291 --> 00:07:25.319
Use the dedicated Python environment to package source, synthetic policies, and pinned dependencies, excluding secrets and evaluation answers.

00:07:25.319 --> 00:07:29.161
Even a local server can make billable model and Search calls.

00:07:29.161 --> 00:07:35.180
Deploy the code into the prepared project and grant only the runtime identity's required roles.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:41.582
Invoke the exact numeric remote version, then compare package contracts, tool outputs, and citations.

00:07:41.582 --> 00:07:48.946
Finally, stop the session compute while keeping the agent and resources according to the approved retention policy.

00:07:48.946 --> 00:07:52.088
Agent Framework is now taught in two focused labs.

00:07:52.088 --> 00:07:57.346
First verify the dedicated Python environment, owned project, and model throughput.

00:07:57.346 --> 00:08:03.053
In sequential execution, inspect whether the drafter's actual answer reaches the reviewer.

00:08:03.053 --> 00:08:10.813
In concurrent execution, policy, budget, and risk roles handle the same question without waiting for one another's output.

00:08:10.813 --> 00:08:16.776
Both patterns together make at most five model calls, with at least one minute between starts.

00:08:16.776 --> 00:08:22.227
Compare roles, actual inputs, answers, tokens, and elapsed time in the evidence files.

00:08:22.227 --> 00:08:30.692
Collecting responses is not automatic consensus; this exercise calls neither a real stock function nor a purchasing approval system.

00:08:30.692 --> 00:08:35.481
This module compares revision after review with a change of responsible agent.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:40.394
Reuse the preceding environment setup; completing its paid runs is not required.

00:08:40.394 --> 00:08:44.623
Group chat speaks three times: drafter, reviewer, then drafter again.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:49.723
Read the final drafter's answer, not the system notice that the conversation ended.

00:08:49.723 --> 00:08:54.761
Handoff requires an actual delegation tool call followed by a specialist response.

00:08:54.761 --> 00:09:01.105
Together these patterns allow at most seven model calls without increasing termination or token limits.

00:09:01.105 --> 00:09:05.708
Choose a pattern using the actual revised sentences and transferred inputs.

00:09:05.708 --> 00:09:10.808
Neither local orchestration implements human approval or remote A2A communication.

00:09:10.808 --> 00:09:16.162
Store only one fictional preference: synthetic user A prefers table-formatted answers.

00:09:16.162 --> 00:09:18.870
Do not use personal or employee information.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:25.295
Create the memory store, record the item identifier, and search separately in user A and user B scopes.

00:09:25.295 --> 00:09:27.878
A should retrieve that item; B should not.

00:09:27.878 --> 00:09:32.980
A table-formatted natural-language answer alone does not prove memory persistence.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:36.192
Item time-to-live differs from the store's lifetime.

00:09:36.192 --> 00:09:38.838
Delete an item only with separate approval.

00:09:38.838 --> 00:09:45.578
Under a no-deletion policy, report storage and isolation separately from the unperformed deletion exercise.

00:09:45.578 --> 00:09:48.077
A routine determines when an agent runs.

00:09:48.077 --> 00:09:55.768
Use the server-side file-search agent, distinguishing a disabled routine's manual dispatch from a genuine one-shot timer.

00:09:55.768 --> 00:10:04.229
Schedule one execution two minutes ahead, then verify the unique input marker, completed response, and trace within the bounded wait.

00:10:04.229 --> 00:10:09.164
Creation success or manual dispatch cannot substitute for scheduled execution.

00:10:09.164 --> 00:10:14.612
An empty CLI history page does not prove nothing ran; inspect the actual action trace.

00:10:14.612 --> 00:10:17.111
Finally, read back enabled equals false.

00:10:17.111 --> 00:10:22.880
Creating an Autopilot account or sending external messages is outside this timer exercise.

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:27.138
Start enterprise governance with the synthetic local cache exercise.

00:10:27.138 --> 00:10:33.112
Observe the two expected failures: a denied user and a revoked user can still read cached data.

00:10:33.112 --> 00:10:37.943
Move authorization ahead of the cache return, then rerun the unchanged tests.

00:10:37.943 --> 00:10:41.438
Do not change the permitted-user list to make them pass.

00:10:41.438 --> 00:10:46.904
Next, distinguish developer, project identity, agent runtime, and end-user permissions.

00:10:46.904 --> 00:10:51.608
Document network, gateway, and document-access responsibilities separately.

00:10:51.608 --> 00:10:58.218
Passing the local exercise does not establish that real Azure roles or document permissions were tested.

00:10:58.218 --> 00:11:04.677
CI/CD is an elective for deployment and operations owners, not a prerequisite for learning core features.

00:11:04.677 --> 00:11:10.018
Reproduce the local error that promotes a candidate merely because execution completed.

00:11:10.018 --> 00:11:16.353
Repair only the function to also require a quality pass, zero critical failures, and zero missing rows.

00:11:16.353 --> 00:11:19.397
Publishing and version management belong here too.

00:11:19.397 --> 00:11:25.856
Runnable agent version, active version serving users, and Teams app Publish version are different values.

00:11:25.856 --> 00:11:32.377
Actual publishing and recovery require supported tools, organizational permissions, and separate approval.

00:11:32.377 --> 00:11:35.483
Never invent a previously approved recovery target.

00:11:35.483 --> 00:11:38.961
Finish with resource and cost review in module nineteen.

00:11:38.961 --> 00:11:44.746
Whether you finish only the core course or choose advanced labs, end with this shared wrap-up.

00:11:44.746 --> 00:11:47.296
Closing the browser does not stop billing.

00:11:47.296 --> 00:11:54.139
Within the approved scope, stop only sessions and routines you created, then read back those exact identifiers.

00:11:54.139 --> 00:11:58.431
Learners who ran only local functions do not need Azure stop commands.

00:11:58.431 --> 00:12:05.958
Retained resources may continue incurring Search, logging, and storage charges; empty billing rows do not prove zero cost.

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:09.068
Record a retention owner and next cost-review time.

00:12:09.068 --> 00:12:11.868
Delete only separately approved exact targets.

00:12:11.868 --> 00:12:15.538
Resetting browser progress does not remove Azure resources.
